# smtpd_sender_login_maps — source of truth: deploy/postfix/sender_login.pcre
#
# An authenticated submission client may only use an envelope sender on
# mail.odile.fyi (which is also the only domain OpenDKIM signs), or the one
# apex identity the support mailbox owns. The value is the SASL login that owns
# it. There is one tenant account today; M1 replaces this table with one row per
# tenant.
#
# help@odile.fyi is the address Savio sends as from Thunderbird. It is allowed
# for the login that is the same string, and it is rewritten by
# sender_canonical.pcre onto mail.odile.fyi before the queue, so SPF is still
# evaluated on the domain whose record authorises this host. The generic line
# below still means "any other mail.odile.fyi sender belongs to odile-test".
/^help@odile\.fyi$/           help@odile.fyi
/^[^@]+@mail\.odile\.fyi$/   odile-test
